1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,800
Every AI reply sounds the same.
Polite, tidy, nothing like you.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:06,800
My friends would spot it in a second.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,300
This is SaySo, a keyboard
that writes the way you'd say it.

4
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:14,600
I type a plain draft,
tap the sparkle,

5
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:18,500
and get versions in my own voice.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
And I don't send one long paragraph,
I send bursts.

7
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:26,500
So SaySo does too: a stack.

8
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:30,700
Tap, send. Next. Send.

9
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,800
Setting it up is one tap.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,300
Then a friend asks for help on Saturday,
and I can't.

11
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,500
I double-tap the back of my phone,

12
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:46,300
say who it's for and add a note:
politely decline.

13
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,000
Three replies, the way I would.

14
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:54,700
Pick one, it's copied.
Paste, send.

15
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,800
In the app's chat it's the same voice.

16
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:03,000
A story comes back the way I'd actually send it:
in a few messages, each one copyable.

17
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:05,800
Other versions fold into stacks.

18
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:12,700
And it remembers the thread:
"in English" changes this answer.

19
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:15,800
My voice comes from my own writing.

20
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:20,000
Chats teach how I text:
SaySo asks which one is me

21
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:24,000
and tests itself on messages
it hasn't seen.

22
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:28,000
Emails and essays are their own kinds:

23
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:34,700
my sent emails teach how I greet and sign off,
never what they said.

24
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:39,000
Now an essay. I paste the question
and just talk.

25
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:42,000
Muse Voice Transcribe writes it down;

26
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:48,500
SaySo writes it in my formal voice,
only from my facts, at the length I asked.

27
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:53,500
Then it asks what would make it stronger.

28
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:58,700
Emails too.

29
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,800
Too long? Thumbs down.

30
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:05,600
It rewrites, and remembers the rule
for next time.

31
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:10,700
Everything it learns is listed,
and I can forget any of it.

32
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:13,500
Under the hood, four Meta models.

33
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:17,300
Muse Spark Open, open weights,
writes in my style.

34
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,300
Muse Spark 1.3 reads.

35
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:21,600
Muse Voice Transcribe listens.

36
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:26,500
My own LoRA on Muse Glimmer is trained,
waiting for a GPU.

37
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:32,800
In a blind test, five friends guessed right
53% of the time.

38
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:37,700
Chance is 50%.

39
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:40,700
Only my own writing is stored.

40
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:45,800
Other people's messages, screenshots and voice notes
are read, then dropped.

41
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:49,500
SaySo.
Your words, your voice.

42
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:53,700
And you always press send.
